{"text":"SQL fundamentals"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Data visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Ideally complete:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"1 CTD/dossier project"},{"text":"1 regulatory submission tracker"},{"text":"1 PV-regulatory dashboard"},{"text":"1 regulatory intelligence project"},{"text":"1 post-approval change assessment"},{"text":"1 relevant industry internship"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning for this particular career is:"},{"type":"p","text":"“B.Pharm graduate with integrated expertise in Regulatory Affairs, Pharmacovigilance and Pharmaceutical Data, with practical knowledge of CTD/eCTD, GMP/GCP/GVP, CMC, regulatory intelligence, lifecycle management, Excel, SQL and regulatory data systems.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The major advantage of this specialization is its hybrid nature."},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of positioning solely as a documentation-oriented Regulatory Associate, the student should develop into a:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Regulatory","Safety","Data professional"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"with three complementary capabilities:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Pharmaceutical Knowledge","Regulatory Expertise","Data & Digital Capability"]},{"type":"p","text":"That combination provides a strong foundation for long-term progression into Global Regulatory Affairs, CMC Regulatory Affairs, Regulatory Intelligence, RIM, PV-Regulatory, and Regulatory Technology roles."}]}]}